      "worked": "Using the any-order property, pair the numbers as $(1+100), (2+99), \\ldots, (50+51)$. There are 50 pairs, each with sum 101.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}1+2+\\cdots+100&=50\\times101\\\\1+2+\\cdots+100&=5050\\end{align*}$$",
